{"id":"n-20261016-rh5ko1","category":"sports","display_title":"Broncos Beat Seahawks In Overtime","display_title_he":"הברון קטנו ניצחון על הסיאהוקס בהארכה","short_summary":"The Denver Broncos defeated the defending Super Bowl champion Seattle Seahawks 17-14 in overtime following a decisive 53-yard field goal.","english_level":"C1","words":481,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/oct/16/seahawks-broncos-nfl-thursday-night-football","title":"Super Bowl champions slump again as Darnold’s picks cost Seahawks against Broncos","published_at":"2026-10-16T04:00:03.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-16T04:00:03.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-16T06:00:32.182Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The defending Super Bowl champion Seattle Seahawks experienced another setback, dropping their record to three wins and three losses after a tense 17-14 defeat against the host Denver Broncos in an overtime thriller on Thursday night. This latest result means the visiting team has already matched its entire loss total from the previous championship-winning campaign, having now fallen for the second time in the span of five days.","Throughout the contest, the defensive units largely dominated the field, fulfilling a strategy that Broncos linebacker Alex Singleton highlighted after the game by stating that it was precisely a defensive battle and the way they wanted it to finish on top. The Broncos managed to establish an early advantage during the second quarter, thanks to rushing touchdowns from both JK Dobbins and RJ Harvey. Despite dealing with a severely injury-riddled roster and an inconsistent offense, Denver ultimately emerged victorious from a grueling six-week opening stretch of the season, establishing a solid four-win and two-loss record. However, their offensive production on the night was remarkably minimal, accumulating just 168 yards of total offense and punting on every single possession in the second half, excluding a final one-play kneel-down.","Quarterback Bo Nix contributed by completing 17 of his 27 passing attempts for 107 yards, while Dobbins led the rushing attack with 41 yards on 17 attempts, and Harvey added three receptions for 31 yards. On the opposing side, Seattle quarterback Sam Darnold endured a difficult evening, completing 27 of 51 passes for 278 yards, zero touchdowns, and two crucial interceptions. Wide receiver Jaxon Smith-Njigba provided a bright spot for the Seahawks by hauling in 12 receptions for a total of 134 yards, while teammate Emanuel Wilson added 52 rushing yards on 14 carries.","The game grew increasingly dramatic late in the fourth quarter. Seattle narrowed the deficit when George Holani punched in a one-yard touchdown run around the right end with 5:41 remaining, followed closely by a successful two-point conversion pass from Darnold to Rashid Shaheed in the back of the end zone to pull the visitors within 14-11. Shortly afterward, Denver appeared poised to seal the win when Kris Abrams-Draine intercepted Darnold at the Denver 31-yard line with only 1:25 remaining in regulation. Yet, the Denver offense failed to make progress, going three-and-out while burning a mere 28 seconds off the clock.","A subsequent 31-yard punt return by Shaheed granted Seattle excellent field position at their own 46-yard line. Taking advantage of the opportunity, Darnold orchestrated a swift drive that positioned kicker Jason Myers to nail a dramatic 34-yard field goal with a mere three seconds left on the clock, forcing the game into an extra period.","Ultimately, the decisive moment in overtime arrived when Denver defender Ja'Quan McMillian intercepted another pass from Darnold, this time at the Seattle 43-yard line. This critical turnover paved the way for Wil Lutz to step onto the field and successfully execute a 53-yard field goal, sealing a hard-fought defensive victory for the home team."],"facts":[{"fact":"The Denver Broncos defeated the Seattle Seahawks 17-14 in overtime on Thursday night.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Wil Lutz kicked a 53-yard field goal in overtime to secure the Broncos' win.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The winning kick was set up by Ja'Quan McMillian intercepting a pass from Sam Darnold at Seattle's 43-yard line.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Broncos finished a tough six-week stretch with a 4-2 record despite injuries and offensive struggles.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Seahawks dropped to 3-3, matching their total losses from the previous season when they won the Super Bowl.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"JK Dobbins and RJ Harvey scored second-quarter rushing touchdowns for Denver.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Denver managed just 168 yards of total offense and punted on all six second-half possessions outside of a kneel-down.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Bo Nix completed 17 of 27 passes for 107 yards for the Broncos.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Sam Darnold completed 27 of 51 passes for 278 yards with no touchdowns and two interceptions.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Jaxon Smith-Njigba recorded 12 receptions for 134 yards for Seattle.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Jason Myers tied the game with a 34-yard field goal with three seconds left in regulation after Rashid Shaheed's 31-yard punt return.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"George Holani scored on a one-yard rushing touchdown in the fourth quarter, followed by a two-point conversion pass to Shaheed.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"defending","lemma":"defend","pos":"verb","he":"מגן","name":false},{"text":"Super Bowl","lemma":"Super Bowl","pos":"noun","he":"סופרבול","name":true},{"text":"champion","lemma":"champion","pos":"noun","he":"אלופה","name":false},{"text":"Seattle Seahawks","lemma":"Seattle Seahawks","pos":"noun","he":"סיאטל סיהוקס","name":true},{"text":"experienced","lemma":"experience","pos":"verb","he":"חווה","name":false},{"text":"setback","